<h1>Localiser Probe Calibration - Metris MCA</h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p class="description"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">Localiser Probe Calibration is necessary to maintain a high degree of accuracy.</span></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Run KUBE. Enter</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold; font-style:italic;"><i><b>System &gt; Hardware Settings</b></i></span><span lang="EN-GB">. Go to ”Localiser” page and press <a href="../Hardware/MMD/Settings/hardware_settings_-_localiser_(Metris_MCA_advanced_settings).htm">“Advanced Settings...”</a> button. In the MetrisMCA advanced settings dialog choose "</span>Probe settings..." button, then in the dialog <a href="../Hardware/MMD/Settings/hardware_settings_-_localiser_(Metris_MCA_advanced_settings).htm#Probe_settings">"Probe settings"</a> press "Calibrate" button.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p class="stepstitle">Step1: Choose calibration methods</p>
<p>Three main methods for probe calibration are available:</p>
<table cellspacing="0" class="whs4">
<col>
<col>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td class="whs6">
<p class="sub-head">Cone calibration with static points</p>
<p>This probe calibration method is available for hard and floating probes only.</p>
<p>It consists of capturing static points in an inner cone in 3 directions, the user will be guided by a wizard.</p>
<p>The points are collected by single pressing on one of the capturing buttons</p>
</td>
<td class="whs7">
<p class="normal-table"><img src="Images/calibr_st.png" width="402px" height="270px" border="0" class="img_whs8" alt=""></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td class="whs9">
<p class="sub-head">Cone calibration with dynamic points</p>
<p>This probe calibration method is available for hard and floating probes only.</p>
<p>It consists of capturing stream points in an inner cone in 3 directions, the user will be guided by a wizard.</p>
<p>The points are collected by pressing and holding one of the capturing buttons.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle">Limitation angle</p>
<p class="parameterdescription" style="margin-right:0px;">For the dynamic points method a value for angle limit is required. This parameter defines the max angle for capturing points downwards in each direction. Its value could vary between 5 and 90 degrees.</p>
</td>
<td class="whs10">
<p class="normal-table"><img src="Images/calibr_d.png" width="402px" height="270px" border="0" class="img_whs8" alt=""></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td class="whs11">
<p class="sub-head">Sphere calibration</p>
<p>This method is available for all probe types.</p>
<p>It consists of capturing static points on a sphere.</p>
<p>The points are collected by single pressing on one of the capturing buttons (hard and floating probes) or by touching the sphere surface (electronic probes).</p>
<p class="parameterstitle">Sphere diameter</p>
<p class="parameterdescription" style="margin-right:0px;">If sphere calibration method is chosen, then it is required to use a sphere with known diameter. Type the diameter value (in mm) in the "sphere diameter" field, then continue the wizard.</p>
</td>
<td class="whs10">
<p class="normal-table"><img src="Images/calibr_sph.png" width="402px" height="270px" border="0" class="img_whs8" alt=""></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p class="parameterdescription">&#160;</p>
<p class="stepstitle">Step2: Calibration procedure</p>
<p>For each calibration method the main window displays visible instructions how to capture data (current position, current direction, number of captured points, etc). To start capturing data the following conditions should be fulfilled:</p>
<ol>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps">the probe calibration piece/certified sphere mounted on a stable surface;</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps">the arm initialised</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps">correct probe tip mounted on the arm</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps">correct settings input at the previous steps of calibration wizard</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p>For capturing points the user can press one of the following buttons:</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">the front button of the handgrip</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">the red button of the arm</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">the buttons on the probe</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">touching the sphere surface (for electronic probes only)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="steps">For deleting points the user can press one of the following:</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">the side button of the handgrip</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">the blue button of the arm</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Note"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span>: The delete button will reject the last captured point for sphere and static points methods. For dynamic points method it will reject the whole set of points of the last direction.</p>
<p>&#160;</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-CClick">
<p class="Click">&#160;Click on the link below to see detailed description of the different wizards:</p>
</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet" style="text-decoration:underline;"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Cone</b></span> calibration with <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>static points</b></span></a></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP164066663" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p class="parameterdescription"><img src="Images/calibr_st1.png" width="402px" height="270px" border="0" class="img_whs8" alt=""></p>
<ol>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps">Place the probe in the inner cone of the probe calibration piece.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps">Position the arm so , that the last arm axis is vertically oriented. The target position is displayed by the probe tip on the picture above. The current position of the last arm axis is displayed by the red line on the picture. Ideally the current position should fit to the target position.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps">Press the red arm button to take the first point. The information in the dialog is updated instantly and the captured point position is coloured in green on the window.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<ol start="4">
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps">Incline the handgrip at 45degrees (see the new target position of the probe tip) and get the second point. The red arc indicates the direction of probe movement when capturing points.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps">Incline the handgrip at 90 degrees and get the third point.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p class="Note"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span>:<br>
The target positions for the probe are exemplary, larger position tolerances are accepted.</p>
<ol start="6">
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps">Repeat the steps 2 to 5 for all specified directions. &#160;For each direction 15 points are required</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps">When the last point is captured, the result is automatically calculated and displayed. The <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Finish</b></span> button becomes enabled.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p class="parameterdescription">&#160;</p>
</div>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet" style="text-decoration:underline;"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a2" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Cone</b></span> calibration with <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>dynamic points</b></span></a></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP163777969" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p class="parameterdescription"><img src="Images/calibr_d1.png" width="402px" height="270px" border="0" class="img_whs8" alt=""></p>
<ol>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps">Place the probe in the inner cone of the probe calibration tip.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps">Position the arm so , that the last arm axis is vertically oriented. The start/end target positions are marked by the blue lines on the picture above. The start angle position is predefined and the end angle position is set by the user at step 1 of the wizard. The current position of the last arm axis is displayed by the red line on the picture.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps">Press and hold the red arm button. Incline the handgrip down while holding the red button to capture data (follow the red arc direction). The information in the dialog is updated instantly. All captured points on the arm track are coloured in green. If some positions are not taken, the user can go back and recapture the missing section only.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<ol start="4">
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps">Repeat steps 2 and 3 for all specified directions. 200 captured points are required for each direction.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps">When the last point is captured, the result is automatically calculated and displayed. The <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Finish</b></span> button becomes enabled.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p class="parameterdescription">&#160;</p>
</div>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet" style="text-decoration:underline;"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a3" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Sphere</b></span> calibration</a></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP165601833" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p class="parameterdescription"><img src="Images/calibr_sph1.png" width="402px" height="270px" border="0" class="img_whs12" alt=""></p>
<ol>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps">Place the probe on the sphere as shown above - first position in first direction. The target position is defined by the probe model on the picture above. Touch the surface (electronic probe) or press the capture button to get the first point.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps">Move the probe consequently to capture the required points for the first direction (as shown by the transparent probe images on the picture). Please, follow also the guiding text on left.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<ol start="3" type="1" class="whs13">
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps">Repeat steps 1 and 2 for all the required directions. For each direction 9 points are required</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p class="parameterstitle">Directions description:</p>
<p><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>First</b></span> =&gt; The points should be captured perpendicular to the surface and around the sphere equator (see picture above).</p>
<p><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Second and fourth</b></span> =&gt; The points should be captured perpendicular to the surface and following two perpendicular sphere meridians (see picture below).</p>
<p><img src="Images/calibr_sph2.png" width="402px" height="270px" border="0" class="img_whs14" alt=""></p>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Third and fifth</b></span> =&gt; The points should be captured tangential to the surface and following the same perpendicular sphere meridians as for direction 2 and 4 (see picture below).</p>
<p><img src="Images/calibr_sph3.png" width="402px" height="270px" border="0" class="img_whs14" alt=""></p>
<ol start="4" type="1" class="whs13">
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps">
<p class="steps">When the last point is captured, the result is automatically calculated and displayed. The <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Finish</b></span> button becomes enabled.</p>
</li>
</ol>
</div>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="parameterdescription">&#160;</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">For an acceptable probe calibration the result <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Standard deviation</b></span> should have value of 0.05 or below.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">If you are satisfied with the results, then press the <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Finish</b></span> button.</p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a4" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example for result window</a></p>
